========== STAGE 21 EVIDENCE REVIEW ==========
TX submission action pointer: [queue + 0x20]
legacyDequeue passes owner, queue, packet-slot pointer, requested count, and refCon; then calls the action pointer.
legacyDequeue tests EAX; zero means no progress; nonzero EAX is accumulated and used to advance ring slots.
listDequeue calls the same five-argument action pointer; EAX is accumulated and subtracted from outstanding slots.
Therefore TX action return is a packet count, not an IOReturn error status.
The distinct 3-argument query-free-space handler at [queue + 0xF0] is not the TX submission action.
Stage21's original BLOCKED label was a runner classification bug: it searched method paths for METHOD_FILE instead of checking the collected assembly files. The disassembly files were present.

